  "body": "## What changed\nThe closed 2D contour already takes a user-set start point (#1478) and exit point (#1492) through the project file and MCP `edit_operation`. The GUI had no door to them. This PR adds that door, as typed coordinates:\n\n- The 2D Contour \"Lead in / Lead out\" tab has two new optional groups, \"Start point\" and \"Exit point\". Each group is switched on in its header, like Plunge and Engagement.\n- Each group has an X row and a Y row in model coordinates (\"Start X\", \"Start Y\", \"Exit X\", \"Exit Y\").\n- One visible line under the rows says the safety rule: a point that the lead cannot fit at is refused by name, and the point never moves.\n- Off writes `None`, which is the automatic seam (the same as every earlier file). On seeds the model origin.\n- The rows edit the draft params. Apply commits them through `EditOperationParams`, so Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y restore the earlier point.\n- Other kinds draw neither group. They refuse a point by name (`OpParams::named_refusal`), so a row there could only produce a refusal.\n\nNew file `crates/ui/src/egui_app/start_exit_rows.rs` (74 lines) and one call in `approach_page.rs`. No change to the generator, a command, the project file or MCP.\n\n## Images\nRendered with the real page code in an `egui_kittest` harness (a 2D Contour with a start point of X12.5 Y-20 in its params). \"Before\" is this branch with the one new call removed, which is the page code of main.\n\nLead in / Lead out tab, before: ![](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/8b952e0f9bdcc7cf4285643e2efad18b14c1a83a/issue-1448/before-lead-tab.png?raw=true)\n\nLead in / Lead out tab, after: ![](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/8b952e0f9bdcc7cf4285643e2efad18b14c1a83a/issue-1448/after-lead-tab.png?raw=true)\n\n## Tests\nNew `crates/ui/src/egui_app/start_exit_tests.rs` (4 tests, structural: AccessKit labels, roles, toggled and enabled state):\n- `the_contour_lead_tab_has_both_point_groups_off_by_default`: both groups are on the tab, their header switches are off and enabled, the X/Y rows are not in the tree, and drawing the tab writes no point.\n- `a_typed_start_point_applies_through_the_history_and_undoes`: the switch seeds (0, 0) and shows the rows and the consequence line. A typed X of 12.5 edits only the draft. Apply commits (12.5, 0) and leaves the exit unset. Undo gives `None` again, and redo gives (12.5, 0) again.\n- `switching_the_exit_point_off_clears_it`: a saved exit shows its group on with its rows; the switch off writes `None` and removes the rows.\n- `kinds_without_a_picked_start_draw_neither_group`: 2D Pocket and Face draw neither group.\n\nUpdated `every_field_lives_on_exactly_one_section`: \"Start point\" and \"Exit point\" are on the Contour's Lead tab only.\n\nReadings:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on 91e51a2db: green. ui lib 820 passed, 6 ignored (snapshot lane); `boundary` 3, `boundary_picks` 6, `sinker_setup` 2, `theme_files` 14 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nOutput with no point set: unchanged. This PR touches no generator, post or project-file code, so the goldens are the same by construction; the gate selected no app, motion or post suite.\n\n## Project file and MCP\n- Project file: no new field (the fields shipped in #1478 and #1492). No version bump.\n- MCP: no new command. `edit_operation` already takes `links.approach.start_point` and `exit_point`.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The pixel snapshot lane (release only; no PNG changed).\n- A generate from the GUI after Apply. The generator law for a picked point is pinned by the motion `contour_start` and app `contour_start_point` suites, which this PR does not touch.\n- Inch display: the rows use the shared `num` unit lens, the same as every other length row.\n\n## Left for later\n#1473 holds the rest: the viewport pick on the wall (item 2), compensation (4), open chains (5), tilted contours (6) and other operations such as the Pocket entry point (7). Item 3 (tabs) is PR #1822. This PR uses `Refs`, so #1448 stays open.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1448-start-exit-rows.md`.\n\nChangelog: The 2D Contour's Lead in / Lead out tab has Start point and Exit point groups, where you type the X and Y at which the cut starts and leaves the closed contour.\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #1448\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
